  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN. Each element of AAA is 0,1,0, 1, 0,1, or 222.\n\nYou can perform the following operation as many times as you like:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i&lt;∣A∣1 \\leq i &lt; |A|1≤i&lt;∣A∣), delete AiA_iAi​ and Ai+1A_{i+1}Ai+1​ from the array, and insert (Ai+Ai+1) mod 3(A_i + A_{i+1}) \\bmod 3(Ai​+Ai+1​)mod3 in their place.\n\nNote that this operation reduces the length of AAA by 111.\nDefine f(A)f(A)f(A) to be the lexicographically minimum†^\\dagger† possible array that AAA can be transformed into using this operation several (possibly, zero) times.\n\nAlso define val(A)\\text{val}(A)val(A) to be the ternary value of the array AAA. Formally,\n\nval(A)=∑i=1NAi⋅3i−1\\text{val}(A) = \\sum_{i=1}^N A_i \\cdot 3^{i-1}val(A)=i=1∑N​Ai​⋅3i−1Your task is to compute\n\n∑i=1N∑j=iNval(f(A[i…j]))\\sum_{i=1}^N \\sum_{j=i}^N \\text{val}(f(A[i\\ldots j]))i=1∑N​j=i∑N​val(f(A[i…j]))where A[i…j]A[i\\ldots j]A[i…j] denotes the subarray of AAA from index iii to index jjj, i.e. the array [Ai,Ai+1,…,Aj][A_i, A_{i+1}, \\ldots, A_j][Ai​,Ai+1​,…,Aj​].\n\nThe answer can be large, so compute it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n†^\\dagger† An array PPP is said to be lexicographically smaller than another array QQQ if and only if one of the following holds:\n\n\nPPP is a prefix of QQQ, but P≠QP \\neq QP=Q; or\nThere exists an index iii such that Pi&lt;QiP_i &lt; Q_iPi​&lt;Qi​, and Pj=QjP_j = Q_jPj​=Qj​ for all 1≤j&lt;i1 \\leq j &lt; i1≤j&lt;i.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the value of &nbsp;∑i=1N∑j=iNval(f(A[i…j]))\\ \\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^N \\sum_{j=i}^N \\text{val}(f(A[i\\ldots j]))&nbsp;i=1∑N​j=i∑N​val(f(A[i…j])), modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤20 \\leq A_i \\leq 20≤Ai​≤2",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
